Subject: [PATCH] Automated analysis after fieldwork: the plan runs itself, the
 findings are read, the hypotheses judged (research intelligence, Phase 5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 2 wrote the analysis plan before fieldwork and the analytics package
could run every planned item — but results were recomputed on request and
never kept, nothing judged a hypothesis, nothing ran by itself, and the
copilot saw no results. Now:

packages/analytics/src/findings.ts (new): findingsFor reads each result
structurally — the tests' p-values and effect sizes, a regression's
coefficient table (intercept left out, terms resolved back to variables,
direction kept), a correlation's r and p, the NPS KPI, the reliability
table — never the insight sentences — into findings with their evidence
(test, statistic, p, effect, n) and a strength on the usual scales; a
crosstab yields one finding per banner variable with the largest gap as
detail; a small base carries the caution, an empty one is a placeholder.
hypothesisVerdicts judges each H1, H2… from the analyses planned for it:
supported / not supported / mixed / inconclusive (small base, or only
descriptives — with what to add) / untested, each with its reason; a
crosstab's banner counts as evidence only when the hypothesis names the
variable, a planned test pairs the same two, or it is the only banner.
runPlan executes the whole plan on one dataset (saved "Planned"
refinements replace the engine's definition by planned id), ranks the
findings, gives the verdicts and the chart each result is best shown as;
compactRun is what is stored; briefText is the run in a few lines for the
copilot; nextMilestone names the fieldwork milestone due — first readable
base (30), halfway to target, target, end of field — once each.

Studio: migration 0046 analytics_runs; lib/analytics runPlanFor /
latestRun / listRuns / dueMilestone; analytics route GET plan/latest,
GET plan/runs, POST plan/run (audited: analytics.plan_run); the hourly
cron /api/cron/analysis-runs runs due milestones for live surveys with a
plan (analysisPlan.autoRun, on unless false). The copilot: findingsIntent
and the FINDINGS GUIDE (answer from the run's numbers only; quote test,
p, effect, base; a verdict is the run's; "none yet" without a run; "not
tested" plus the analysis action that would test it); the outline carries
the run's brief on findings and analysis turns; the hook loads the latest
run (and a test seam) and sends verdicts and the strongest findings with
every turn; Intelligent → Findings: verdicts with reasons (an untested
hypothesis offers Plan a test through the copilot), findings strongest
first with evidence, significant-only toggle, the run's trigger/time/base,
the milestone due, Run the plan now, Ask the copilot to narrate, Open in
Analytics.

Tests: analytics findings.test.ts (4; 37 mutations, 37 caught); studio
copilot.test.ts (+1; 6/6); browser scripts/findings-copilot-test.mjs (6
checks; 11/11 against the Studio surfaces). Analytics 222, engine 1424,
import 28, Studio 223; findings, analysis-framework, copilot,
quota-copilot, translation-copilot, ux-copilot, intelligent-mode and
analytics browser suites green. Docs: docs/AUTOMATED-ANALYSIS-2026-10-05.md.

